---This page provides information on the available methods and properties for drawing 3D shapes in the game world.
---
---For a general introduction, see the Shapes page.
---
---The `ShapeList` table allows plugins to draw shape data arrays and ShapeData objects in the game world.
---
---It also manages the creation and destruction of ShapeInstances and ShapeEntities, which in turn draw themselves to
---the game world.
---@class ShapeList
ShapeList = {}

---Draws a shape in the game world using the provided `settings` table of values.
---
---Supported values for the `settings` table are:
---
---Shape data can be provided via settings in the following priority order:
---
---Only the highest priority setting with valid data is drawn; any lower priority settings with data are ignored.
---@param settings ShapeListDrawSettings A table of key-value pairs which describe the settings for the draw operation.
function ShapeList.Draw(settings) end

---Draws a segmented line in the game world using the provided `settings` table of values.
---
---This method does not require line indices, like those found in a ShapeData. Instead, it draws a line from each
---provided position to the next.
---
---Supported values for the `settings` table are:
---@param settings ShapeListDrawLineSettings A table of key-value pairs which describe the settings for the draw operation.
function ShapeList.DrawLine(settings) end

---Creates a new ShapeInstance with the given name. Returns `nil` if an instance already exists with that name.
---
---Info: Only one instance can exist with the same name in each plugin. However, separate plugins can have an instance
---with the same name, as shown below:
---@param name string The name of the instance.
---@return ShapeInstance? # The created ShapeInstance. Returns `nil` if the instance could not be created.
function ShapeList.CreateInstance(name) end

---Returns an existing ShapeInstance with the given name. Returns `nil` if no instance exists with that name.
---@param name string The name of the instance.
---@return ShapeInstance? # The ShapeInstance which was found. Returns `nil` if no instance was found.
function ShapeList.GetInstance(name) end

---Returns a list of all existing ShapeInstances created by the plugin.
---@return ShapeInstance[] # All existing ShapeInstances.
function ShapeList.GetAllInstances() end

---Attempts to destroy the given ShapeInstance and returns whether it was successful.
---@param instance ShapeInstance The ShapeInstance object.
---@return boolean # Whether the ShapeInstance was successfully destroyed.
---@overload fun(name: string): boolean
function ShapeList.DestroyInstance(instance) end

---Creates a new ShapeEntity with the given name. Returns `nil` if an entity already exists with that name.
---
---Info: Only one entity can exist with the same name in each plugin. However, separate plugins can have an entity with
---the same name, as shown below:
---@param name string The name of the entity.
---@return ShapeEntity? # The created ShapeEntity. Returns `nil` if the entity could not be created.
function ShapeList.CreateEntity(name) end

---Returns an existing ShapeEntity with the given name. Returns `nil` if no entity exists with that name.
---@param name string The name of the entity.
---@return ShapeEntity? # The ShapeEntity which was found. Returns `nil` if no entity was found.
function ShapeList.GetEntity(name) end

---Returns a list of all existing ShapeEntities created by the plugin.
---@return ShapeEntity[] # All existing ShapeEntities.
function ShapeList.GetAllEntities() end

---Attempts to destroy the given ShapeEntity and returns whether it was successful.
---@param entity ShapeEntity The ShapeEntity object.
---@return boolean # Whether the ShapeEntity was successfully destroyed.
---@overload fun(name: string): boolean
function ShapeList.DestroyEntity(entity) end

---The `ShapeData` table provides a way to store data like positions, colours and triangle and line indices in one
---object.
---
---It also allows those objects to be registered by name and re-used across a variety of drawing operations by object or
---name.
---@class ShapeData
---@field positions Vector3[] A list of 3D positions.
---@field rgba Long[] A list of 32-bit colours. The number of colours in this array must match the number of positions, or be empty. If empty, the default colour value is `0xFFFFFFFF`.
---@field tris integer[] A list of position index triplets which represent a single triangle. Indices are 0-indexed.
---@field lines integer[] A list of position index pairs which represent a single line. Indices are 0-indexed.
ShapeData = {}

---Creates and returns an empty `ShapeData` object.
---@return ShapeData # The newly created data object.
function ShapeData.new() end

---Returns the names of all registered ShapeData that are available to the current plugin.
---@return string[] # An array of registered ShapeData names.
function ShapeData.GetAllRegistered() end

---Returns whether a ShapeData is registered with the given name.
---
---Info: String matches are case-sensitive.
---@param name string The string to match against each registered ShapeData name.
---@return boolean # Whether the name has been registered.
function ShapeData.IsRegistered(name) end

---Registers ShapeData with the given name, and returning whether the registration was successful.
---
---Info: ShapeData objects are copied when registered. This means that changes made to the object after registration do
---not affect the newly registered object data.
---@param name string The string to register as the ShapeData name.
---@param shapeData ShapeData The data to register.
---@return boolean # Whether the ShapeData was successfully registered.
function ShapeData.Register(name, shapeData) end

---Attempts to unregister a ShapeData which is registered with the given name.
---
---Info: String matches are case-sensitive.
---
---Warning: When a `ShapeData` is unregistered, any ShapeInstance or ShapeEntity which uses that data will be
---automatically destroyed.
---@param name string The string to match against each registered ShapeData name.
---@return boolean # Whether the ShapeData was successfully unregistered.
function ShapeData.Unregister(name) end

---The keys `ShapeList.Draw` takes in its table.
---@class ShapeListDrawSettings
---@field shapeDataName string? The name of a registered ShapeData to draw.
---@field shapeData ShapeData? The ShapeData to draw directly.
---@field shapePositions Vector3[]? The raw shape data positions to draw.
---@field shapeRGBA Long[]? The raw shape data colours to draw.
---@field shapeTris integer[]? The raw shape data triangle indices to draw.
---@field shapeLines integer[]? The raw shape data line indices to draw.
---@field translation Vector3? A positional offset transform applied to the shape when it is drawn. Allows shape data constructed in local-space to be drawn in world-space. Defaults to `0,0,0`.
---@field rotation Vector3? A rotational transform applied to the shape when it is drawn. `X = Yaw, Y = Pitch, Z = Roll` Defaults to `0,0,0`.
---@field scale Vector3? A scaling transform applied to the shape when it is drawn. Defaults to `1,1,1`.
---@field ignoreDepth boolean? Controls how the shape handles depth testing when drawing: `true` - Always draws on top of world geometry `false` - Draws behind occluding world geometry. Defaults to `false`.
---@field colour Long? A 32-bit colour which is multiplied against the RGBA data of the shape being drawn. Defaults to `0xFFFFFFFF`.
---@field lineWidth number? The drawn thickness of any lines defined by the shape data. Maximum value is `10.0`. Defaults to `2.0`.
---@field asBillboard boolean? Whether the shape should always rotate to face the camera. This rotation is applied around the centre of final AABB of the drawn shape. Defaults to `false`.

---The keys `ShapeList.DrawLine` takes in its table.
---@class ShapeListDrawLineSettings
---@field positions Vector3[]? The list of positions to draw lines between.
---@field translation Vector3? A positional offset transform applied to the lines when they are drawn. Allows positions constructed in local-space to be drawn in world-space. Defaults to `0,0,0`.
---@field rotation Vector3? A rotational transform applied to the lines when they are drawn. `X = Yaw, Y = Pitch, Z = Roll` Defaults to `0,0,0`.
---@field scale Vector3? A scaling transform applied to the lines when they are drawn. Defaults to `1,1,1`.
---@field ignoreDepth boolean? Controls how the lines handle depth testing when drawing: `true` - Always draws on top of world geometry `false` - Draws behind occluding world geometry. Defaults to `false`.
---@field colour Long? The 32-bit colour to use as the line colour. Defaults to `0xFFFFFFFF`.
---@field lineWidth number? The drawn thickness of the lines. Maximum value is `10.0`. Defaults to `2.0`.

---A `ShapeInstance` is a dynamic object which contains some ShapeData and automatically handles drawing itself in the
---game world.
---
---See Shape Instance for additional information on this object.
---@class ShapeInstance
---@field isValid boolean (Read-only) Whether this instance still exists. Dispose of this usertype object when invalid.
---@field name string (Read-only) The name the instance was created with.
---@field hasData boolean (Read-only) Whether this instance has valid ShapeData or a registered shape name assigned to it.
---@field translation Vector3 (Writeable) A positional offset transform applied to the shape when it is drawn. Allows shape data constructed in local-space to be drawn in world-space. Defaults to `0,0,0`.
---@field rotation Vector3 (Writeable) A rotational transform applied to the shape when it is drawn. `X = Yaw, Y = Pitch, Z = Roll` Defaults to `0,0,0`.
---@field scale Vector3 (Writeable) A scaling transform applied to the shape when it is drawn. Defaults to `1,1,1`.
---@field visible boolean (Writeable) Whether the instance should be drawn. Defaults to `true`.
---@field ignoreDepth boolean (Writeable) Controls how the instance handles depth testing when drawing: `true` - Always draws on top of world geometry `false` - Draws behind occluding world geometry. Defaults to `false`.
---@field colour Long (Writeable) A 32-bit colour which is multiplied against the RGBA data of the ShapeData being drawn. Defaults to `0xFFFFFFFF`.
---@field lineWidth number (Writeable) The drawn thickness of any lines defined by the instance's ShapeData. Maximum value is `10.0`. Defaults to `2.0`.
---@field asBillboard boolean (Writeable) Whether the shape should always rotate to face the camera. This rotation is applied around the centre of final AABB of the drawn shape. Defaults to `false`.
local ShapeInstance = {}

---Assigns a copy of the given shape data to the instance and returns whether the data was valid and successfully set.
---
---This method also clears any value set by SetShapeDataName.
---@param shapeData ShapeData The shape data to copy to the instance.
---@return boolean # Whether the shape data was successfully set on the instance.
function ShapeInstance:SetShapeData(shapeData) end

---Assigns the name of a registered ShapeData to the instance and returns whether the registered name exists and was
---successfully set.
---
---This method also clears any value set by SetShapeData.
---@param shapeName string The name of a registered shape data ShapeData.
---@return boolean # Whether the shape name was successfully set on the instance.
function ShapeInstance:SetShapeDataName(shapeName) end

---Attempts to destroy the instance. Returns `false` if the entity does not exist, otherwise `true`.
---@return boolean # Whether the instance was successfully destroyed.
function ShapeInstance:Destroy() end

---A `ShapeEntity` is an object which contains some ShapeData, is often placed at a fixed coordinate, and automatically
---handles drawing itself in the game world.
---
---See Shape Entity for additional information on this object.
---@class ShapeEntity
---@field isValid boolean (Read-only) Whether this entity still exists. Dispose of this usertype object when invalid.
---@field name string (Read-only) The name the entity was created with.
---@field hasData boolean (Read-only) Whether this entity has valid ShapeData or a registered shape name assigned to it.
---@field coordGrid CoordGrid (Writeable) The coordinate at which the entity is placed. The entity will be placed at the centre of the coordinate, and automatically sets its height to align with the ground. Replaces any value set for `coordFine`.
---@field coordFine CoordFine (Writeable) The coordinate at which the entity is placed. Automatically sets its height to align with the ground. Replaces any value set for `coordGrid`.
---@field visible boolean (Writeable) Whether the entity should be drawn. Defaults to `true`.
---@field ignoreDepth boolean (Writeable) Controls how the entity handles depth testing when drawing: `true` - Always draws on top of world geometry `false` - Draws behind occluding world geometry. Defaults to `false`.
---@field colour Long (Writeable) A 32-bit colour which is multiplied against the RGBA data of the ShapeData being drawn. Defaults to `0xFFFFFFFF`.
---@field lineWidth number (Writeable) The drawn thickness of any lines defined by the entity's ShapeData. Maximum value is `10.0`. Defaults to `2.0`.
---@field alignType ShapeEntityAlignType (Writeable) How the entity's shape data should align with the ground. See ShapeEntityAlignType. Defaults to `NONE`.
---@field heightOffset number (Writeable) How high above the ground level the entity should be drawn. Defaults to `0.0`.
---@field rotation number (Writeable) The starting rotation of the entity. Rotation occurs around the vertical Y axis. Units are in degrees. Defaults to `0.0`.
---@field rotationSpeed number (Writeable) How far the entity rotates in a clockwise direction in one second. Rotation occurs around the vertical Y axis. Units are in degrees. Defaults to `0.0`.
---@field asBillboard boolean (Writeable) Whether the shape should always rotate to face the camera. This rotation is applied around the centre of final AABB of the drawn shape. This setting often conflicts with `alignType` - it is recommended to use `ShapeEntityAlignType.NONE` when drawing a shape entity as a billboard. Defaults to `false`.
---@field drawDistance number (Read-only) The near draw distance for the entity. Use SetDrawDistance() to set the draw distances.
local ShapeEntity = {}

---Assigns a copy of the given shape data to the entity and returns whether the data was valid and successfully set.
---
---This method also clears any value set by SetShapeDataName.
---@param shapeData ShapeData The shape data to copy to the entity.
---@return boolean # Whether the shape data was successfully set on the entity.
function ShapeEntity:SetShapeData(shapeData) end

---Assigns the name of a registered ShapeData to the entity and returns whether the registered name exists and was
---successfully set.
---
---This method also clears any value set by SetShapeData.
---@param shapeName string The name of a registered shape data ShapeData.
---@return boolean # Whether the shape name was successfully set on the entity.
function ShapeEntity:SetShapeDataName(shapeName) end

---Sets the draw distance, in fine units, for the ShapeEntity.
---
---If the distance between the Player Character and the ShapeEntity is greater than `distance` then the entity will not
---be drawn.
---
---The tested distance is the horizontal measurement between the Player Character's world position and the closest point
---on the ShapeEntity's bounding box.
---@param distance number The distance, in fine units, from the Player Character at which the entity will stop drawing.
---@overload fun(self: ShapeEntity, nearDistance: number, farDistance: number)
function ShapeEntity:SetDrawDistance(distance) end

---Attempts to destroy the entity. Returns `false` if the entity does not exist, otherwise `true`.
---@return boolean # Whether the entity was successfully destroyed.
function ShapeEntity:Destroy() end

---Used by the ShapeEntity property `alignType`.
---@enum ShapeEntityAlignType
ShapeEntityAlignType = {
    ---No rotational alignment.
    NONE = 0,
    ---The shape rotates to align with the average slope of the ground.
    OBJECT = 1,
    ---Each separate position in the shape is translated vertically to align with the ground, for a closer fit.
    MODEL = 2,
}
